        <h2>Dosage Guidelines by Experience Level</h2>

        <p>Dosing ketamine nasal spray is not as simple as counting sprays. Absorption through the nasal mucosa is highly variable depending on mucosal blood flow, spray particle size, and whether you have recently used decongestants. The table below provides conservative ranges based on a standard 0.1 mL spray volume delivering approximately 10 mg of ketamine per spray (100 mg/mL concentration).</p>

        <p>Research published in the <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30561100/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Journal of Psychopharmacology</a> confirms that intranasal bioavailability ranges from 25% to 50%, meaning your body absorbs roughly half of what goes up your nose. This variability is why starting low and titrating upward is non-negotiable.</p>

