        <h3>The Titration Method</h3>

        <p>Instead of taking all sprays at once, experienced researchers use the titration method: one spray per nostril, wait 10 minutes, assess effects, then repeat. This approach has two advantages. First, it prevents overshooting your target dose due to delayed absorption. Second, it reduces nasal irritation by distributing the solution across both nostrils rather than flooding one side.</p>

        <p>Never redose within a 60-minute window. Ketamine has a curious dose-response curve where the subjective effects can continue to intensify even after you stop spraying. This is due to gradual mucosal absorption combined with active metabolites like norketamine extending the timeline.</p>

